but I actually just mean it
in the sense of like,

00:08:49.801 --> 00:08:51.534
I'll think of, like, a line.
-Okay.

00:08:51.534 --> 00:08:53.367
-Like you could put in, like,
a haiku or some [bleep].

00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:56.300
And I'll be like, okay,
this will be the song,

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:57.601
and this is where it comes from.

00:08:57.601 --> 00:08:59.033
And sometimes that looks like

00:08:59.033 --> 00:09:02.133
rewriting the song
like a billion times,

00:09:02.133 --> 00:09:03.868
because sometimes
I do get too specific

00:09:03.868 --> 00:09:05.334
and people are like,
you're going to --

00:09:05.334 --> 00:09:06.501
-Yeah.

00:09:06.501 --> 00:09:07.934
-You're going to get
in trouble legally.

00:09:07.934 --> 00:09:10.300
You're going to have problems.
I'm like, "I don't care."

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.300
And I do, I do care.
I care --

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:13.300
I care quite a bit.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.567
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.567 --> 00:09:16.901
But yeah, so it looks
different all the time.

00:09:16.901 --> 00:09:18.901
But I love writing.
-And do you --

00:09:18.901 --> 00:09:20.801
Do you get --
How do you get excited?

00:09:20.801 --> 00:09:22.300
When you realize you have
a song that you love...

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:23.367
-Yeah.

00:09:23.367 --> 00:09:24.367
-Do you get excited
in the process?

00:09:24.367 --> 00:09:25.701
Do you --
Does your sort of

00:09:25.701 --> 00:09:27.033
does your pulse start to race
when you're like,

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:28.400
oh, I think we got a hold
of a good one here.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:29.501
-Oh, I get --
I get so excited.

00:09:29.501 --> 00:09:30.934
Sometimes
I'm so excited that I cry

00:09:30.934 --> 00:09:34.267
because I'm very, like,
I react, like, to music.

00:09:34.267 --> 00:09:36.000
I think a lot of people do,
but like for me

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.801
it's always been very physical.

00:09:37.801 --> 00:09:39.000
Like, I, like,
have little, like,

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.033
twitches and, like, tics
and things like that.

00:09:41.033 --> 00:09:44.033
And I used to feel,
like, very weird about it.

00:09:44.033 --> 00:09:45.467
And now that I work
with, like, pretty much

00:09:45.467 --> 00:09:47.000
the same people
all the time,

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.567
and I work with, like, a lot of
people who are my best friends,

00:09:49.567 --> 00:09:51.701
they, like, see me, like,
tic and like twitch

00:09:51.701 --> 00:09:53.467
and, like, start to cry
and, like, hyperventilate.

00:09:53.467 --> 00:09:54.968
And they're like,
"Yeah."

00:09:54.968 --> 00:09:56.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.300
-Well,
I'm so happy you're here.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.601
It's such a delight
to meet you.

00:09:59.601 --> 00:10:00.601
And I'm so thrilled you're
sticking around

00:10:00.601 --> 00:10:01.601
and do a song for us.

00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:02.701
-Thanks.
Thanks for having me.

00:10:02.701 --> 00:10:03.868
-Alright, you guys,
that's Reneé Rapp.

00:10:03.868 --> 00:10:04.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:04.968 --> 00:10:06.901
Her album "Snow Angels'
is available now.

00:10:06.901 --> 00:10:08.501
Stick around,
we'll be right back

00:10:08.501 --> 00:10:10.634
with a performance
from Reneé Rapp.

